1
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:04,720
Roman, look.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:09,960
Here I built a Tesla per stalker schematic and a driver for testing coils.

3
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:16,950
There are 5 or 6 turns wound on the Granade.

4
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:25,190
Since there's no generator, I'm taking 1.6 MHz from the driver.

5
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:33,430
Turn on the power.

6
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:39,000
Consumption 0.8 V.

7
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,740
24 V.

8
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:54,020
If you bring a neon bulb close, it starts glowing specifically in this zone.

9
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:01,060
Nowhere else does it glow.

10
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:04,300
Or at the hot end of the wire.

11
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:16,980
If you light a bulb, the lamp lights up.

12
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:38,380
If you take a pyrometer and measure the Granade's temperature around the inductor, it's 35 degrees.

13
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,520
The inductor itself heats up.

14
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:50,680
Then there's a decrease and further increase.

15
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,300
That is, in this spot the Granade starts to heat up.

16
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:06,650
Even more than the inductor itself.

17
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:16,840
At just 0.8 A current, 24 V.

